# Build context excludes for every root-context image (backend, file-service, credential-service,
# web, the Python and Go services that build from `.`).
# Never copy host node_modules into the image: they were created against the host's
# pnpm store, so `COPY . .` would leave the image's modules dir inconsistent and pnpm
# would try to purge+reinstall it (ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY in a
# non-interactive build). The image installs its own deps in the deps/builder stage.
**/node_modules

# Build outputs / caches — regenerated inside the image
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/coverage
# TS incremental build state — MUST be excluded. The @cos/* packages put their
# tsBuildInfoFile at the package root (not in dist), and tsc with `incremental: true`
# skips emit when a stale buildinfo says "up to date". Letting a host buildinfo leak in
# via `COPY . .` makes `tsc` emit nothing → dependents fail with TS2307 on @cos/* dist.
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# VCS
.git
.gitignore

# Local env / secrets — never bake into an image (keep the templates only).
# `**/`, not bare: a bare `.env` matches the context root only, and until 2026-11-12 a local build
# baked backend/.env (46 secret-named keys: database, Redis, Keycloak, AWS, OpenAI, JWT, encryption
# keys, …) and apps/mobile/.env (EXPO_PUBLIC_* only) into every root-context image; the
# services/file-service and apps/web .env are symlinks to the root .env and came in dangling. CI
# was not affected (a clean checkout has no .env); images built on a dev machine were.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Local tool state and agent config — needed by no image (all git-ignored except .claude/, which
# is tracked but copied by no Dockerfile). Without these a local build carried
# infrastructure/terraform's provider downloads (764 MB), the Python services' .venv and caches,
# the pnpm store and .claude into /app.
**/.terraform
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
.pnpm-store
.claude

# Logs / OS cruft
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store

# React Native native build dirs — large, never needed by backend/file-service images
apps/mobile/ios
apps/mobile/android
